.TH geectl-pull-request-merge 1  "geectl-pull-request-merge 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-pull\-request\-merge \- Merge a pull request. On OBS this accepts the submit request; on Gitea it merges the pull request. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl pull\-request merge\fR [\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-\-method\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREFERENCE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Merge a pull request. On OBS this accepts the submit request; on Gitea it merges the pull request. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
The message left with the merge. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a message may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-method\fR \fI<METHOD>\fR
The Gitea merge style (Gitea only; refused on an OBS ref)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
merge
.IP \(bu 2
rebase
.IP \(bu 2
rebase\-merge
.IP \(bu 2
squash
.IP \(bu 2
fast\-forward\-only
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Accept past open reviews (OBS only; refused on a Gitea ref)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREFERENCE\fR>
The pull\-request handle: `obs:<id>` or `gitea:<owner>/<repo>#<number>`
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
